# OSINT workspace — MCP rules (agents must follow)

## Librarian status (2026-06-14)

**`cemini-librarian` is deleted.** `kb_search`, `kb_context`, and `conductor_query` via lazy-tool will **fail**. Query wikis with Read/grep locally. **stash** MCP is red unless tunnel restored — do not block sessions on it. See `wiki/meta/librarian-decommission-2026-06-14.md`.

## Which MCP servers exist here

| Scope | Servers | Notes |
|-------|---------|--------|
| **This folder only** | `lazy-tool`, `prod-mcp`, `exa`, `fetch` | Open **OSINT WORKSPACE** as the workspace root |
| **Global (every chat)** | `stash`, `brave-search`, `playwright` | From `~/.cursor/mcp.json` |

**Home / no folder open:** only global MCP loads. `lazy-tool` will show **off** — that is normal. **stash** may show **red** — expected after librarian decommission (2026-06-14); disable `com.cemini.stash-tunnel` or ignore.

**Do not** look for project servers named `conductor`, `kb-server`, or `librarian-stash` — they are reached **through lazy-tool** only.

### lazy-tool toggle (human step)

If **lazy-tool** shows **Off** in Cursor Settings → Tools & MCP, tell the user to turn it **On**. Agents cannot fix this in chat — the server must be enabled in the UI once (Cursor saves the preference). `.cursor/mcp.json` sets `"disabled": false` but the UI toggle still wins if you previously turned it off.

